  "executive_briefing": "As of August 2026, institutional digital asset market structure is consolidating along regulatory and technological vectors. The Senate's progression of the CLARITY Act (H.R. 3633) is defining regulatory boundaries for digital commodities versus securities, providing institutional capital with long-awaited legal predictability. Concurrently, spot Bitcoin ETFs have surpassed $100B in AUM, evolving from initial accumulation into standard portfolio diversification and treasury management. On the smart contract front, Ethereum maintains its dominant EVM ecosystem for enterprise tokenization and DeFi, but faces emerging competition from Bitcoin-native execution layers and languages like Clarity, which offer predictable, decidable smart contracts anchored directly to Bitcoin. Meanwhile, trustless cross-chain liquidity networks like THORChain are eliminating wrapped asset risks by facilitating direct native BTC-to-ETH swaps.",
